    "result": "A process is a running program. It has its own memory space. A thread is one unit of work inside a process. Threads in the same process share its memory. Processes stay isolated from each other.\n\nThe operating system schedules both. Creating a thread costs less than creating a process. Use threads for work that shares data. Use processes for work that must stay isolated.",
